::SECTION_21_WINDOWS_SERVICES_AND_SCM::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-SVC-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Windows Service Control Manager & Background Daemons (StartServiceCtrlDispatcherW)"
    PHENOMENON      : "Error 1053 (service did not respond in a timely fashion) or `ERROR_FAILED_SERVICE_CONTROLLER_CONNECT` (1063)"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Running heavy initialization inside `ServiceMain` before reporting `SERVICE_RUNNING`, or calling `StartServiceCtrlDispatcherW` when launched interactively from CMD."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Report `SERVICE_START_PENDING` with incremental `dwCheckPoint` hints, transition to `SERVICE_RUNNING` prior to worker loop entry, and support a `--console` CLI flag for interactive execution."
}

::SECTION_22_COM_AND_WMI_TELEMETRY::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-COM-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "COM Apartment Initialization & WMI System Queries (CoInitializeEx / IWbemServices)"
    PHENOMENON      : "`RPC_E_CHANGED_MODE` (0x80010106) failures, `BSTR` / `VARIANT` memory leaks, or silent null-pointer crashes on `IWbemClassObject::Get`"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Mixing `COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED` and `COINIT_MULTITHREADED` on the same thread, omitting `VariantClear()`, or reading `vtVal` without checking `vt != VT_NULL && vt != VT_EMPTY`."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Initialize COM once per thread with `COINIT_MULTITHREADED`, guard every `VARIANT` extraction by checking `FAILED(hr)` and `vt` type tags, and release all interfaces in reverse acquisition order."
}

::SECTION_23_SERIAL_AND_DEVICE_IO::
@FAULT_NODE [ERR-DEV-001] {
    DOMAIN          : "Serial COM Ports & DeviceIoControl Hardware Handles (\\\\.\\COMx)"
    PHENOMENON      : "`CreateFileW` failure on COM10+, indefinite `ReadFile` blocks, or corrupted baud/parity framing"
    ROOT_CAUSE      : "Opening `COM10` without the `\\\\.\\` Win32 device namespace prefix, or failing to configure `COMMTIMEOUTS` and `DCB` structures."
    INVARIANT_RULE  : "Format all port paths as `\\\\.\\COM%u`, configure explicit `COMMTIMEOUTS` (`ReadIntervalTimeout`, `ReadTotalTimeoutConstant`), and purge stale RX/TX buffers via `PurgeComm` upon open."
}

::MASTER_VERIFICATION_GATE::
@GATE_CHECK_F07 {
    23. SCM_STATE_CADENCE  : Emit `SERVICE_START_PENDING` checkpoints, transition to `SERVICE_RUNNING` early, and provide `--console` fallback.
    24. COM_VARIANT_GUARD  : Enforce consistent MTA initialization, validate `VARIANT.vt` before dereferencing, and invoke `VariantClear()`.
    25. DEVICE_NAMESPACE   : Prefix hardware handles with `\\\\.\\` and enforce deterministic `COMMTIMEOUTS` prior to I/O.
}
